1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The Gaussian integral: find the total area under e to the minus x squared.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
There is no elementary antiderivative, but the total area is exact.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Square the integral and use two independent variables.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The resulting Gaussian density is rotationally symmetric.

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Use polar coordinates: the area element is r dr d theta.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Evaluate the radial integral to obtain one half, and the angular integral to obtain two pi.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The original positive integral is the square root of pi.
